    {
      "heading": "H.C. Manoj Kumar Patel vs State Of U.P. on 9 May, 2023",
      "level": 2,
      "content": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Author: Rajeev Misra",
      "level": 3,
      "content": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Bench: Rajeev Misra",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        "Heard Mr. Akhil Ranjan, the learned counsel for applicant and the learned A.G.A. for State.",
        "Perused the record.",
        "This application for bail has been filed by applicant-Manoj Kumar Patel seeking his enlargement on bail in Case Crime No. 215 of 2023, under Sections 419 , 420 , 120B IPC, Sections 66 , 66C of the Information Technology Act, Section 29 of Police Act and Sections 7 / 8 / 13 of the Prevention of Corruption Act, Police Station-Khalilabad, District-Sant Kabir Nagar.",
        "At the very outset, the learned A.G.A. submits that anticipatory bail application of co-accused, Kameshwar Mishra has already been rejected by this Court vide order dated 24.04.2023 passed in CRIMINAL MISC ANTICIPATORY BAIL APPLICATION U/S 438 CR.P.C. No. - 4207 of 2023 ( Kameshwar Mishra Vs. State of U.P ). For ready reference, the same is reproduced hereinunder:-",
        "Learned A.G.A. contends that case of present applicant and aforementioned co-accused is almost similar and identical, therefore, no separation or segregation can be made with regard to the role of the present applicant in the crime in question. He, therefore, submits that bail application of present applicant is also liable to be rejected.",
        "When confronted with above, the learned counsel for applicant referred to the order dated 25.04.2023 passed in Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. 18236 of 2023 ( Virendra Vs. State of U.P. ). For ready reference, the same is reproduced hereinunder:",
        "10. However, it is made clear that any willful violation of above conditions by the applicant, shall have serious repercussion on his bail so granted by this court and the trial court is at liberty to cancel the bail, after recording the reasons for doing so, in the given case of any of the condition mentioned above.",
        "Order Date :- 25.4.2023\""
      ]
    },
